h in engineering, business English in administration, diplomatic English in international relations, media English in journalism and communication, and English applied to digital technologies in computer engineering."}]]}],["$","div",null,{"ref":"$undefined","className":"rounded-lg border bg-card text-card-foreground border-slate-200 shadow-sm","children":["$","div",null,{"ref":"$undefined","className":"p-7","children":[["$","h3",null,{"className":"text-lg font-semibold text-slate-900","children":"A structured progression, from the Licence (Bachelor's degree) to the Master"}],["$","$L25",null,{"type":"single","collapsible":true,"className":"mt-4","children":[["$","$L26","Licence 1",{"value":"niveau-0","children":[["$","$L27",null,{"className":"text-sm font-semibold text-slate-800","children":"Licence 1"}],["$","$L28",null,{"className":"text-sm leading-7 text-slate-600","children":"Consolidation of grammatical and lexical foundations, oral and written comprehension, everyday expression and the acquisition of academic vocabulary."}]]}],["$","$L26","Licence 2",{"value":"niveau-1","children":[["$","$L27",null,{"className":"text-sm font-semibold text-slate-800","children":"Licence 2"}],["$","$L28",null,{"className":"text-sm leading-7 text-slate-600","children":"Development of professional communication, oral presentations, writing and the specialised vocabulary of each field."}]]}],["$","$L26","Licence 3",{"value":"niveau-2","children":[["$","$L27",null,{"className":"text-sm font-semibold text-slate-800","children":"Licence 3"}],["$","$L28",null,{"className":"text-sm leading-7 text-slate-600","children":"Use of English in projects, case studies, presentations, reports and some viva voce defences."}]]}],["$","$L26","Master 1 and Master 2",{"value":"niveau-3","children":[["$","$L27",null,{"className":"text-sm font-semibold text-slate-800","children":"Master 1 and Master 2"}],["$","$L28",null,{"className":"text-sm leading-7 text-slate-600","children":"Strengthening professional and academic English, analysis of specialised documents, presentation of research work, negotiation and communication in an international environment."}]]}]]}],"$L29"]}]}]]}]}]}]
1a:["$","section",null,{"className":"container mx-auto px-6 py-16","children":["$","div",null,{"className":"grid gap-10 lg:grid-cols-2","children":[["$","div",null,{"children":[["$","h2",null,{"className":"text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900","children":"Defences in French and in English"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"mt-4 leading-7 text-slate-600","children":"Viva voce defences are a major instrument of professional readiness and of assessing communication skills. At ABS, they are designed as opportunities to structure an argument, to present results, to answer a jury's questions and to defend one's proposals before an audience. Assessment arrangements may include:"}],["$","ul",null,{"className":"mt-5 space-y-3","children":[["$","li","Defences in French for academic projects and work;",{"className":"flex gap-3 text-sm leading-7 text-slate-700","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"mt-2 size-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-cyan-600","aria-hidden":true}],"Defences in French for academic projects and work;"]}],["$","li","Presentations or defences in English, depending on language level and pathway;",{"className":"flex gap-3 text-sm leading-7 text-slate-700","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"mt-2 size-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-cyan-600","aria-hidden":true}],"Presentations or defences in English, depending on language level and pathway;"]}],["$","li","Bilingual defences, with a presentation in one language and a question-and-answer sequence in the other;",{"className":"flex gap-3 text-sm leading-7 text-slate-700","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"mt-2 size-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-cyan-600","aria-hidden":true}],"Bilingual defences, with a presentation in one language and a question-and-answer sequence in the other;"]}],["$","li","Executive summaries, abstracts or presentation materials in English;",{"className":"flex gap-3 text-sm leading-7 text-slate-700","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"mt-2 size-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-cyan-600","aria-hidden":true}],"Executive summaries, abstracts or presentation materials in English;"]}],["$","li","Simulations of meetings, negotiations, conferences and job interviews in French and English.",{"className":"flex gap-3 text-sm leading-7 text-slate-700","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"mt-2 size-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-cyan-600","aria-hidden":true}],"Simulations of meetings, negotiations, conferences and job interviews in French and English."]}]]}],["$","p",null,{"className":"mt-5 text-sm leading-7 text-slate-500","children":"The precise arrangements are defined in the curricula and assessment regulations. The progression is adapted to the level of study so that the language requirement serves as a learning objective rather than an unjustified obstacle to assessing disciplinary knowledge."}]]}],["$","div",null,{"children":[["$","h2",null,{"className":"text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900","children":"English tailored to each speciality"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"mt-4 leading-7 text-slate-600","children":"To bring bilingualism to life in practice, ABS encourages the progressive use of French and English in the teaching activities of all fields: documentary reading, bilingual presentations, international case studies, literature research, debates and professional simulations."}],["$","div",null,{"className":"mt-6 overflow-hidden rounded-2xl border border-slate-200","children":["$","table",null,{"className":"w-full text-sm","children":[["$","thead",null,{"className":"bg-slate-50 text-left text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-slate-500","children":["$","tr",null,{"children":[["$","th",null,{"className":"px-5 py-3","children":"Field"}],["$","th",null,{"className":"px-5 py-3","children":"English"}]]}]}],"$L2a"]}]}]]}]]}]}]
